DEVIATIONS / DECISIONS
1. Spec item 5 "App Attest: Apple DeviceCheck verify (server-side)":
   implemented as the Apple DeviceCheck token validation endpoint
   (api.devicecheck.apple.com/v1/validate_device_token, ES256 JWT client
   auth, hand-rolled, no new deps). Full App Attest DCN (CBOR + Apple root
   CA) remains a documented 501 stub; provider name: "devicecheck".
2. Paths kept at /api/v1/auth/attest{,/nonce,/verify} (repo convention);
   /verify added as canonical route, bare /attest kept for older clients.
3. Replay/expired nonce now answers 401 (spec) instead of 400; response
   gains attested:true and nonce response gains expires_at. Client body
   field platform_token accepted (token kept as legacy alias); server-side
   GetDel binding retained, optional nonce cross-check added.
4. Discovery hard gate applies to GET /api/v1/radar and
   POST /api/v1/dating/swipe; skipped when provider is unset/log so local
   dev and CI stay green. Nonce rate limit: 5/hour/user (device identity
   is only known after verification, so the limit keys on the
   authenticated principal).
